  }}
/>

## The three problems

**`parser`: the shared parser reads every date month first.** All our tenants write the day
first, so 7 April comes out as 4 July. This is the bug #4471 names and the fix that is queued.
It comes in through the app, email and the booking-v2 form.

**`hint`: booking-v3 prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under its date field.** Alder Physio, Copper Studio and
Pale Harbour run booking-v3. Their people type what the hint tells them, month first, and the
form reads it the tenant's way, day first. The symptom looks the same as `parser`, a swapped day
and month, but the parser fix does not touch it: only reports that came through the v3 form
belong here. The form's hint, or the way it reads the field, needs its own change.

**`one-day`: the date moves by one day, not by a swap.** Tuesday 12 May shows as Monday 11 May
(R-41202). A client in Lisbon got Tuesday and one in Toronto got Monday for the same meeting
(R-41344). An invite arrived before its booking (R-41236). Every June booking was one day off
(R-41209). These read as a time-zone shift. The desk already noted them as one-day moves, then
filed them under `parser` by tenant. No parser or hint fix moves a date back by one day.

## How this was counted

- One id, one report: the export has rows twice where its pages overlap.
- The cause comes from the tenant and the way in (`causes.ts`), not from the intake tag. Intake
  guessed from the reporter's browser and got many of them wrong.
- One-day moves are the desk's own list (`desk-notes.json`), checked against every body: they are
  the only reports whose dates differ by one day and not by a day/month swap.
- Subjects say nothing about the cause. Five subjects turn up under all three problems, which is
  why merging by subject ([decision 0001](/kb/decisions/0001-dedupe-by-subject)) put
  them in one ticket.

## What changes for the desk

- #4471 stays the `parser` ticket. Close it when the parser fix ships, not before: then check
  that new booking-v3 form reports and one-day moves still arrive, and file them under their own
  tickets.
- Before merging a date report, ask two things the subject cannot tell you: did it come through
  a booking-v3 form, and did the date swap or move by one day?

